WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.985
Video can reveal people, routines, homes, workspaces, vehicles, and operations.

00:00:04.985 --> 00:00:16.907
A responsible program begins with purpose limitation: define the legitimate safety, security, or operational need and collect only the coverage and detail required for that purpose.

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:18.857
Respect privacy expectations.

00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:26.877
Avoid private or unrelated areas, unnecessary audio, and wider fields of view than the use case needs.

00:00:26.877 --> 00:00:30.129
Use masking or zones when possible.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:38.148
Provide consent, notice, or signage where applicable, and obtain appropriate legal and policy review for the location.

00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:42.267
Set retention by need rather than storage capacity.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:51.587
Keep routine footage and AI metadata only as long as justified, with longer retention for documented events when policy permits.

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:57.006
Deletion should include copies, exports, and backups under a defined lifecycle.

00:00:57.006 --> 00:01:02.425
Restrict live view, search, export, configuration, and administrative access by role.

00:01:02.425 --> 00:01:07.410
Use audit logs to record access, changes, sharing, and deletion.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:15.430
Protect review outcomes because labels and notes may be sensitive even when the original clip is gone.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:25.617
Do not use the system for harassment, covert stalking, inappropriate surveillance, or attempts to identify private individuals without lawful and legitimate authority.

00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:32.336
Model descriptions should not be treated as facts about character, intent, or protected traits.

00:01:32.336 --> 00:01:41.223
Publish clear policy, train reviewers, provide a way to report misuse, and review new use cases before enabling them.

00:01:41.223 --> 00:01:50.977
Local processing can reduce external data exposure, but responsible use still depends on transparency, access control, limited purpose, and human accountability.
